MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OpenCode gets the same one-click Connect as Claude Code, Codex and Claude
Desktop. It merges opencode.json and opencode.jsonc from its config folder
($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/opencode, else ~/.config/opencode); Connect adds
"meridian" (a local MCP server: Meridian --mcp-bridge) to the "mcp" of
opencode.json only, keeping every other key and the first old file as
opencode.json.meridian-backup. opencode.jsonc is never touched; an
opencode.json with comments is left alone and the person is told what to
add. Found when opencode is on the login PATH or its config folder exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
